    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132-a1-a2">

                <pb facs="0297" n="257" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg257"/>

                <head>Lieutenant Colonel Babcock to General Grant</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Headquarters Armies oF the United
                                States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">City Point, Virginia,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 19, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I hereby certify that the accompanying fuzes were captured in Fort Fisher, at the
                    mouth of Cape Fear river, North Carolina, a work held by the so called
                    confederate forces, and captured by the Union forces under Major General A. H.
                    Terry, United States army, and Rear-Admiral D. D. Porter, United States navy,
                    January, 1865.</p>
                <p>These fuzes were used in the vast number of subterranean and submarine mines at
                    that place. I understand that these fuzes are used extensively throughout the
                    so-called southern confederacy.</p>
                <p>Accompanying this are samples of the fuzes, marked A, B, and C, with my name at
                    tached.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>O. E. BABCOCK,<hi rendition="#italic">Lieutenant Colonel and A. D.
                            C.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Lieutenant General <hi rendition="#small-caps">U. S. Grant</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Commanding Armies United States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
